%% States of one CSV row inside one import request.
%% Every path ends in exactly one terminal state, and nothing goes back:
%% a row is never probed after it was classified against existing data,
%% and never inserted after a failed probe. That ordering is what makes a
%% re-run cheap (existing rows cost no Drive probe) and what guarantees a
%% row that failed a check is never written.
%% There is no transition into "updated": an existing video is never changed.
stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> Parsed
  Parsed --> failed: invalid id / empty name / duration <= 0
  Parsed --> skipped: filename seen earlier in chunk
  Parsed --> Classified: fields ok
  Classified --> skipped: same filename, same Drive id in DB
  Classified --> conflict: same filename, other Drive id in DB
  Classified --> failed: Drive id owned by another filename
  Classified --> Probed: new
  Probed --> failed: Drive unreachable / not a video
  Probed --> Inserting: 206 video/*
  Inserting --> inserted: ok
  Inserting --> skipped: 23505 on filename (concurrent add)
  Inserting --> failed: 23505 on drive_file_id / other DB error
  inserted --> [*]
  skipped --> [*]
  conflict --> [*]
  failed --> [*]
